WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.067
This week's checklist.

2
00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:06.333
Concrete moves for the next seven days, wherever you are in the study path.

3
00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:08.607
There are eight moves.

4
00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.267
The first four are about building.

5
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.767
Here is what to build.

6
00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:14.375
Run vLLM locally.

7
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:21.300
Serve a small Llama or Qwen, and watch PagedAttention and continuous batching in the logs.

8
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.833
Build one agentic RAG system with LangGraph and Qdrant, where the agent decides when to retrieve.

9
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:32.367
Design an eval pipeline with your own metrics, and justify every one.

10
00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:36.000
And start one MCP server over a real database.

11
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.067
The other four are about being seen.

12
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:44.100
Create one properly structured repo, with an architecture diagram at the top.

13
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.987
Write one technical post.

14
00:00:45.987 --> 00:00:49.033
Teaching forces precision and builds visibility.

15
00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:50.274
Join the rooms.

16
00:00:50.274 --> 00:00:53.033
Lurking is fine, being present is the point.

17
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:55.099
And target the right companies.

18
00:00:55.099 --> 00:00:57.833
For twenty five lakh and up, skip service firms.

19
00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.267
One closing thought.

20
00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:07.100
Your background as a solution architect, founder and field service expert is not a gap to apologize for.

21
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.733
It is the context most engineers lack.

22
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:12.400
So the formula is simple.

23
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.900
Build the projects.

24
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.333
Measure everything.

25
00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:16.900
Publish the evidence.

26
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.156
Then price yourself accordingly.

27
00:01:19.156 --> 00:01:24.900
The market has more roles than qualified people, and evidence is the only currency it accepts.

28
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.113
Let's recap.

29
00:01:27.113 --> 00:01:32.600
Four moves to build: vLLM, agentic RAG, evals, and an MCP server.

30
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.700
Four moves to be seen: a repo, a post, the right rooms, and the right companies.

31
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.333
Your background is context, not a gap.

32
00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:44.133
Build the projects, measure everything, and publish the evidence.
